    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The legacy European payments and automation business entered 2025 with improving traction—sequential revenue gains and margin expansion pointed to strengthening client demand. That momentum was overlaid mid-year by the acquisition of a larger but declining entity, creating a combined global platform that now faces persistent top-line contraction. While gross margins continue to expand, the demand environment remains mixed, and the transaction introduced integration-related strains that have weighed on operating cash generation.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership executed a transformative acquisition and rebranding, framing the combined entity as a hyper-automation and digital-transformation platform. Efforts are centered on margin protection and cost discipline, with management highlighting normalized profitability measures as top-line pressures linger. The integration has been burdened by one-time cash outflows tied to deal costs and pre‑petition liabilities, casting the near‑term as a stabilization and cleanup phase rather than a growth cycle. The narrative is one of navigating a deliberate transition.",
